{"kind":"assert","text":"FW-1, cause for 9c41c15a: neither name resolution nor the TLS server name. celld has no deployment yet, and it holds requests open until one arrives.\n\nEvidence (22:01Z, curl with --cacert ~/dap-tls/cert.pem):\n- TLS completes for all three names. localhost, 127.0.0.1 and hakuin.local each reach Caddy on :443 over TLS 1.3, and the certificate matches each name (hakuin.local resolves to ::1 locally).\n- https://localhost/ answers 200 with content-length 0 and server Caddy in 2 ms. localhost is not in the Caddyfile site block (\"hakuin.local\", \"127.0.0.1\", as dap-host.json hosts sets), so Caddy answers its empty default. That 200 does not come from the service.\n- https://127.0.0.1/ and https://hakuin.local/ (and /health on each) match the site and reverse_proxy to 127.0.0.1:28900. They time out at 8 s.\n- celld listens on 127.0.0.1:28900 and accepts TCP, but HTTP to it directly times out at 8 s too. Its log says: \"no deployment yet; run `celld deploy` and the node serves it without a restart\" (awaiting_initial_deployment).\n\nExpected: the same requests answer once deploy.py deploys the first project. I will record the result after that step. For docs/self-host-mac.md: before the first deployment, a request through Caddy hangs rather than fails, and an unlisted name such as localhost gets an empty 200 from Caddy. Neither shows the host's health. Read health after deployment, at a listed name.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}